================================================================================
5. Geospatial data sources
================================================================================

No third-party geospatial data is redistributed in this repository. Every layer
below is fetched or supplied by the user at run time. See DATA.md for the full
data availability statement, per-layer provenance, and redistribution status.

Barbados Geoportal — Lands and Surveys Department, Government of Barbados
  Building footprints, telecommunications infrastructure, transport, water and
  wastewater networks, and vulnerability grids.
  Attribution required. Redistribution status is under review; see DATA.md.

Copernicus / Sentinel-2 — European Space Agency / European Union
  https://scihub.copernicus.eu
  Copernicus Sentinel data. Free, full and open licence.

Copernicus GLO-30 Digital Elevation Model — European Space Agency
  https://spacedata.copernicus.eu
  Referenced by the study wizard as a recommended open DEM source.

ESA WorldCover — European Space Agency
  https://esa-worldcover.org
  CC BY 4.0.

Global Forest Change (Hansen et al.) — University of Maryland
  https://glad.earthengine.app/view/global-forest-change
  CC BY 4.0. Cite: Hansen, M. C., et al. (2013), "High-Resolution Global Maps
  of 21st-Century Forest Cover Change", Science 342, 850-853.

OpenStreetMap / Geofabrik extracts
  https://www.openstreetmap.org  |  https://download.geofabrik.de
  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0.
  Any derived database distributed onward must also be ODbL.

OpenCellID
  https://opencellid.org
  CC BY-SA 4.0.

Terrain Tiles on AWS Open Data
  https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/
  Elevation tiles ("terrarium" encoding) fetched at run time by
  examples/data/fetch_open_scene.py. Open data; the underlying SRTM, GMTED and
  3DEP sources are public domain. No API key is required and no tile is
  redistributed here.

TeleGeography submarine cable data
  https://www.submarinecablemap.com
  Used for reference context. Subject to TeleGeography's terms; not
  redistributed here.

PeeringDB
  https://www.peeringdb.com
  CC BY 4.0.
